WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.190
I desired peace

00:03.780 --> 00:09.780
<i>Those born with the Evil Eye, able to see 
shades, cannot hope for a peaceful life.</i>

00:11.090 --> 00:13.850
<i>After my parents sold me 
to the court sorcerers,</i>

00:14.650 --> 00:18.820
<i>I strode the battlefield as a necromancer.</i>

00:20.320 --> 00:24.790
<i>Until the empire fell, in fact.
 Though all that time...</i>

00:25.700 --> 00:28.600
<i>I always, always...</i>

00:31.210 --> 00:33.120
<i>wished to live quietly.</i>

00:34.940 --> 00:36.780
<i>I desired peace.</i>

00:49.700 --> 00:51.210
<i>I didn't care if it was false</i>

00:53.600 --> 00:55.100
<i>or if I was playing make-believe.</i>

00:56.920 --> 01:04.620
<i>I simply longed for the peaceful 
life I could only dimly recall.</i>

01:06.010 --> 01:07.080
<i>Peace.</i>

01:08.450 --> 01:11.710
<i>I wanted peace.</i>

01:16.020 --> 01:19.010
<i>That was all. And yet...</i>

01:20.730 --> 01:22.300
They are defiled.

01:22.750 --> 01:24.890
Annihilate their souls!

01:24.890 --> 01:28.100
Let not the necromancer 
enslave their spirits!

01:28.340 --> 01:31.070
Save them! Save them!

01:31.410 --> 01:34.610
Save these impure children!

01:42.430 --> 01:44.750
<i>The more I sought it, 
the more distant it became.</i>

01:46.620 --> 01:49.170
<i>I initiated my vengeance then and there,</i>

01:49.650 --> 01:52.130
<i>played out over the course of a century.</i>

01:52.340 --> 01:56.800
We were wrong! Please, save us!

01:56.800 --> 01:59.260
Save us! Save us!

01:59.510 --> 02:02.160
Save our miserable souls!

02:02.160 --> 02:05.350
Please, just kill us already!

02:06.080 --> 02:10.900
<i>Soon, my abandoned coal mine was 
a labyrinth crawling with corpses.</i>

02:11.450 --> 02:17.250
<i>Perhaps the soldiers' screams and 
my dark magic attracted them.</i>

02:18.420 --> 02:21.740
<i>Even so, I desired peace.</i>

02:23.130 --> 02:28.080
<i>So I waited for decades, then centuries.</i>

02:28.650 --> 02:31.080
<i>I could no longer die a 
natural death, so I awaited</i>

02:31.540 --> 02:33.420
<i>the coming of one who could slay me.</i>

02:34.610 --> 02:38.270
<i>And my secret art of reincarnation succeeded.</i>

02:39.730 --> 02:46.270
<i>That's why I can't let myself die here,
 when I don't even know what's happening!</i>

02:48.580 --> 02:52.830
She went down so easily? 
It was just one stab through the gut!

02:52.830 --> 02:57.190
Doesn't she have a healing potion?! 
Or an item imbued with curative spells?!

02:59.460 --> 03:00.780
This is awful.

03:00.780 --> 03:06.040
I killed her before I could 
even ask what continent I'm on.

03:06.040 --> 03:10.070
No, ensuring my safety comes first.

03:10.460 --> 03:14.250
I can't even prove I was defending 
myself from an assassin.

03:14.840 --> 03:19.760
I can't lead a peaceful life if I'm 
on the run from the city watch!

03:19.770 --> 03:21.220
Wait!

03:21.470 --> 03:26.190
I said, "Now, let us continue," to a <i>corpse</i>!

05:02.930 --> 05:04.740
Argh!

05:05.280 --> 05:08.850
Has my brain seriously blown a fuse?

05:10.270 --> 05:11.500
<i>Hello.</i>

05:11.500 --> 05:15.280
<i>I'm surprised you're taking so long. 
Did you run into more trouble?</i>

05:15.280 --> 05:17.050
Hey, Clarissa.

05:17.480 --> 05:19.710
Forget trouble, 
this is a total system crash.

05:20.000 --> 05:22.090
<i>I'll send you the video file now.</i>

05:22.090 --> 05:23.210
Video of what?

05:23.210 --> 05:25.590
Watch it, and you tell me.

05:27.340 --> 05:32.310
Have I gone nuts, or has Shinjuku?

05:34.530 --> 05:35.900
Misaki?

05:36.680 --> 05:37.920
Misaki?

05:42.320 --> 05:44.610
Misaki's so cute.

05:44.610 --> 05:46.800
She sure smiles a lot, doesn't she?

05:47.180 --> 05:49.030
There's nothing wrong with smiling.

05:49.030 --> 05:52.730
I'm sure your smile will make people happy.

05:53.360 --> 05:55.650
Find your happiness with everyone...

05:57.160 --> 05:59.800
Mi... sa... ki.

06:10.580 --> 06:13.690
Hey, remember me?

06:13.690 --> 06:16.520
Y-You're Zaki!

06:16.520 --> 06:18.890
Zaki the Killer Killer!

06:18.890 --> 06:21.360
Hm... Right answer,

06:21.670 --> 06:23.610
but not quite the one I'm looking for!

06:24.790 --> 06:30.290
Damn it! You may be Clarissa's pet, 
but you can't get away with—

06:28.720 --> 06:31.160
Clarissa hired me for this.

06:31.390 --> 06:36.200
She said you've done too much killing 
on the side lately, so you need to go!

06:36.710 --> 06:41.110
You looked like you just <i>loved </i>
killing people when I saw you.

06:41.110 --> 06:42.420
How about now?

06:42.420 --> 06:45.630
Are you happy getting killed by me?

06:45.630 --> 06:50.760
I wonder if I look as happy 
now as you did back then.

06:51.000 --> 06:54.220
Don't tell me... you're Sakimiya's...?

06:54.220 --> 06:57.050
I-Is this about revenge?!

06:57.050 --> 07:02.480
Or do you think you're some kind of hero, 
only going after hit men and yakuza?!

07:02.480 --> 07:04.110
Because you're dead wrong!

07:04.110 --> 07:07.030
No way! It's nothing like that!

07:07.030 --> 07:09.780
You see, watching you made me wonder:

07:09.780 --> 07:13.000
Is killing people really that fun?

07:14.060 --> 07:18.200
I kill killers because it seems like fun.

07:18.200 --> 07:19.910
It's as simple as that.

07:22.800 --> 07:27.220
But now that you mention it,
 I've never checked

07:27.780 --> 07:30.630
if I can kill good people, too.

07:32.440 --> 07:34.500
Are you a good person?

07:34.500 --> 07:36.430
Y-Yeah, I'm—

07:45.580 --> 07:48.000
As if.

07:49.180 --> 07:52.410
That must be her. Assassin Zaki.

07:52.410 --> 07:55.310
I hear she's a psycho who kills with a smile.

07:55.310 --> 07:58.160
What's Clarissa-san see in a brat like her?

07:58.160 --> 08:01.120
Polka Shinoyama

07:59.330 --> 08:01.120
You want this job?

08:01.580 --> 08:04.680
But he's not a killer. 
He's just a normal kid.

08:04.680 --> 08:06.330
I know. It's fine.

08:06.680 --> 08:11.550
I already achieved my goal in life,
 so I want to find out

08:11.770 --> 08:15.050
just how messed up I really am.

08:21.920 --> 08:24.060
I killed him, no problem!

08:24.440 --> 08:26.520
I kind of figured

08:26.520 --> 08:31.060
I could kill good people 
just as easily as bad ones!

08:35.370 --> 08:38.990
Welp, I guess someone like 
me's better off dead, huh?

08:39.470 --> 08:42.500
Having me around won't make <i>anybody</i> happy.

08:42.900 --> 08:47.790
Not bad people or good people 
or Clarissa or Kurupon or Hagane-chan.

08:47.790 --> 08:51.670
Probably not even me!

08:52.010 --> 08:57.340
And the only thing I haven't 
tried yet is killing <i>myself</i>.

09:06.510 --> 09:07.770
Hello?

09:07.770 --> 09:09.520
<i>It's me, Kuruya.</i>

09:09.520 --> 09:11.490
What's up, Kurupon?

09:11.490 --> 09:14.490
I was just getting to the climax of my life.

09:14.490 --> 09:16.250
<i>Yeah, I saw.</i>

09:17.240 --> 09:18.740
Oh, hey there.

09:18.740 --> 09:22.490
<i>Die if you want, but finish your job first.</i>

09:22.760 --> 09:23.510
Huh?

09:23.950 --> 09:28.430
<i>The kid whose throat you just slit is 
walking around like nothing happened.</i>

09:28.430 --> 09:30.520
Huh?! Wait, for real?!

09:30.520 --> 09:33.130
You mean I <i>couldn't</i> kill him?!

09:33.130 --> 09:37.140
<i>Looks like it. You've still got a job to do.</i>

09:38.840 --> 09:42.090
<i>Wait... what's going on?</i>

09:42.550 --> 09:46.060
<i>Didn't I just have that 
conversation with Kurupon?</i>

09:47.060 --> 09:53.410
<i>Oh, I get it. That was my 
life flashing before my eyes.</i>

09:54.030 --> 09:56.740
Good, you're awake.

09:57.050 --> 09:58.480
It worked.

10:00.250 --> 10:00.990
Huh?!

10:01.520 --> 10:05.200
How?! Didn't I get skewered 
through the tummy?!

10:06.690 --> 10:09.690
I, um... died, right?

10:09.690 --> 10:11.320
How come I'm alive again?

10:11.320 --> 10:14.210
Well, you aren't, actually.

10:14.210 --> 10:16.840
You could say you've been
 reborn through magic.

10:16.840 --> 10:18.470
So, next question...

10:18.890 --> 10:21.160
What's going on here?

10:25.700 --> 10:27.520
Clarissa?!

10:27.520 --> 10:30.600
What's Clarissa the intermediary doing—

10:30.600 --> 10:31.780
Whoa!

10:32.520 --> 10:34.890
Okay. You're cold.

10:36.430 --> 10:39.040
And you have no pulse whatsoever.

10:39.040 --> 10:40.110
Huh?

10:40.110 --> 10:41.070
Don't worry!

10:41.660 --> 10:43.950
You're 100% dead.

10:43.950 --> 10:46.940
In this language, you're, um...

10:47.650 --> 10:49.870
I've got it! You're a zombie.

10:51.210 --> 10:52.150
Huh?

10:53.810 --> 10:56.560
How's it going, kids?

10:56.560 --> 11:00.180
This is just a text file I'm 
typing with my free hand.

11:00.180 --> 11:02.230
But if you're reading it,

11:02.230 --> 11:05.100
I've probably lost my mind.

11:06.640 --> 11:09.100
<b>40 minutes before Misaki Sakimiya wakes up</b>

11:09.610 --> 11:14.820
I'm Takumi Kuruya, an all-around 
great guy based in Shinjuku.

11:15.350 --> 11:19.910
I'm in business as sort of an info broker,
 using the net and my drones.

11:19.910 --> 11:22.410
Oh, I haven't got flight 
clearance for them, obviously.

11:22.620 --> 11:28.250
For reasons I won't get into, 
I also help some hit men hide bodies.

11:28.630 --> 11:31.950
Anyway, I'd say I've lived 
a discreet and humble life,

11:32.580 --> 11:35.690
and I wanted to keep it that way.

11:37.030 --> 11:38.800
So how'd I end up in this mess?

11:39.620 --> 11:44.240
I'm sorry for interrupting your date,
 Polka Shinoyama-kun.

11:44.240 --> 11:45.720
That <i>is</i> your name, yes?

11:46.050 --> 11:49.180
Before I introduce myself, 
I'd like to ask you a question.

11:49.980 --> 11:52.330
Would you care to explain <i>that</i>?

11:55.350 --> 11:57.360
Takumi-kun, what am I looking at?

11:57.360 --> 12:01.820
<i>That's not me. It must be the 
drone I lost control of earlier.</i>

12:02.050 --> 12:04.900
And can drones fly without making noise?

12:04.900 --> 12:06.240
<i>No way in hell.</i>

12:06.560 --> 12:08.370
Please wait a moment.

12:08.580 --> 12:10.250
I'm about to fix her.

12:17.060 --> 12:21.800
Takumi-kun, I'm guessing you didn't 
whip up these special effects?

12:21.800 --> 12:25.510
<i>If I could make CGI like that, 
I'd do it for a living.</i>

12:27.550 --> 12:30.020
She should wake up soon.

12:30.810 --> 12:33.980
Now, who are all of you?

12:35.120 --> 12:38.440
We're friends of Misaki-chan there.

12:38.810 --> 12:44.650
We came to finish her job and avenge her...
 or at least, that <i>was</i> the plan.

12:45.410 --> 12:48.220
May I take it that she's still alive?

12:48.220 --> 12:51.560
Well... that's a bit of a tricky question.

12:52.300 --> 12:58.000
I didn't do much, but her brain and soul
 are intact and I mended her body.

12:58.250 --> 13:03.920
She just needs a sorcerer to cast 
resurrection magic on her when she wakes up.

13:05.650 --> 13:06.280
Um...

13:07.580 --> 13:09.450
Resurrection magic?

13:10.170 --> 13:11.310
Magic.

13:11.310 --> 13:14.470
Yes? I'm certain this body knows it, too.

13:14.920 --> 13:17.560
You know, R*ise, Ar*se, and so on?

13:17.560 --> 13:19.640
Those are spells from video games.

13:20.130 --> 13:21.780
Video games?

13:22.750 --> 13:27.720
Um... Does this country have magic? 
Practitioners of the spirit arts?

13:27.720 --> 13:31.620
You're the first one I've ever seen.

13:31.620 --> 13:33.410
And other lands?

13:33.410 --> 13:36.260
Plenty of self-proclaimed magicians, 
but that's all.

13:36.260 --> 13:39.580
What about the Olnaql Rzcver 
or the Xvatqbz bs Alnavyq?

13:40.260 --> 13:44.550
Never heard of them. How did 
you pronounce that?

13:52.660 --> 13:54.720
You just had a mass hallucination.

13:54.720 --> 13:56.720
Do you think you can fool us?

13:56.720 --> 13:58.740
Hallucinations are no laughing matter.

14:00.980 --> 14:02.400
Would you please allow yourselves

14:03.190 --> 14:04.490
to be fooled?

14:06.200 --> 14:08.130
Monster!

14:10.900 --> 14:13.020
You know, I don't have a clear grasp

14:14.030 --> 14:18.780
of just how fragile and 
easily killed you are.

14:25.800 --> 14:27.920
Whatever shall I do?

14:28.910 --> 14:31.510
Would you give me a moment to think it over?

14:31.510 --> 14:33.220
You think he'll be that easygoing?

14:33.220 --> 14:35.450
<i>Very well. I'll wait.</i>

14:35.450 --> 14:36.430
You will?!

14:36.430 --> 14:38.930
Has this guy never heard of tension?

14:39.390 --> 14:42.420
Or is he just that confident?

14:43.390 --> 14:49.380
<i>Their weapons remind me of the Imperial 
Dazzling Corps. Talk about creepy.</i>

14:49.950 --> 14:54.170
<i>I'm not sure I have enough 
mana to fight </i>or<i> flee.</i>

14:55.080 --> 14:57.120
<i>Hmm... What should I do?</i>

14:58.780 --> 14:59.460
Hm?

15:00.610 --> 15:01.670
It's close.

15:03.160 --> 15:05.630
I hear them strangely often lately.

15:07.060 --> 15:11.340
There's a fire in the Shakuzawa Building. 
I'll send you my camera feed.

15:12.490 --> 15:14.300
The Shakuzawa Building?

15:14.860 --> 15:17.270
I'm concerned for the children,

15:17.740 --> 15:20.980
but I suppose we'll have to leave 
this to the fire department.

15:29.380 --> 15:31.700
What did that panel show?

15:32.650 --> 15:34.780
A fire. What else?

15:35.400 --> 15:38.040
And who are these children you fear for?

15:38.410 --> 15:42.160
There's an unlicensed nursery 
in the Shakuzawa Building.

15:42.160 --> 15:48.050
It looks after yakuza orphans and 
kids whose mothers work the nightlife biz.

15:50.460 --> 15:53.300
Please take me there immediately.

15:54.180 --> 15:57.640
If you don't know the way, 
they must be strangers to you.

15:57.640 --> 15:59.770
Why do you care?

16:00.430 --> 16:02.890
I've been burned a number of times.

16:04.920 --> 16:10.360
It is... quite painful. Children 
should not suffer such agonies.

16:13.530 --> 16:17.530
Fine. Takumi-kun, show him the way.

16:17.530 --> 16:18.450
<i>Say what?!</i>

16:18.450 --> 16:22.160
A-Are you nuts?! What if 
he makes a break for it?!

16:22.710 --> 16:25.170
That's why I want you to keep an eye on him.

16:31.550 --> 16:32.790
It's over that way.

16:32.790 --> 16:33.930
<i>H-Hey!</i>

16:37.390 --> 16:39.350
<i>W-Wait up!</i>

16:44.190 --> 16:48.480
<i>What the hell?! He didn't go this 
wild when he was running from Misaki!</i>

16:51.180 --> 16:51.940
<i>There it is!</i>

16:52.210 --> 16:53.150
<i>That's the building!</i>

17:03.620 --> 17:07.520
<i>I can use magic to amplify my Evil Eye now.</i>

17:11.820 --> 17:15.050
<i>I still sense the children's life force.</i>

17:15.050 --> 17:19.250
<i>Hey, what's your plan? Firefighters 
and onlookers have this place sur—</i>

17:21.890 --> 17:23.100
<i>What the...?!</i>

17:25.980 --> 17:27.030
Hm?

17:27.030 --> 17:29.510
Did something just jump into the fire?

17:29.510 --> 17:31.440
Huh? Beats me.

17:38.230 --> 17:42.370
Are these your children?

17:43.500 --> 17:46.540
In that case, would you lend me a hand?

17:57.500 --> 18:00.930
Whoa. This fire's spreading <i>way</i> too fast.

18:00.930 --> 18:03.590
H-Hey! There's something up there!

18:03.590 --> 18:04.180
Huh?

18:04.180 --> 18:06.650
What <i>is</i> that?

18:11.000 --> 18:12.840
Dad?

18:22.260 --> 18:27.200
<i>It was hot before, but now 
it's not. It doesn't hurt.</i>

18:29.690 --> 18:33.560
<i>That's Dad's hand. It's so warm.</i>

18:47.710 --> 18:51.510
Did you just see something wild in the smoke?

18:57.150 --> 19:00.160
Yamaty@Shinjuku
Huge skeleton hand
What the hell? lol

18:58.170 --> 19:01.140
In the end, everyone made it out okay.

19:00.220 --> 19:04.370
Tamachan
Skeletons walked through the fire?!

19:01.140 --> 19:04.370
But who does that in front of a crowd?!

19:04.370 --> 19:08.890
And he just jumped out of the building, 
the same as he went in!

19:10.490 --> 19:13.410
Still, what are his morals, anyway?

19:14.390 --> 19:17.670
He treats Misaki's life like a toy one minute

19:18.220 --> 19:20.250
and saves a bunch of kids the next.

19:21.110 --> 19:23.090
It doesn't add up.

19:23.640 --> 19:26.920
I can't figure him out. 
I can't guess what he's thinking.

19:27.800 --> 19:30.550
He seems different from us, somehow.

19:32.620 --> 19:34.170
I'm telling you, Clarissa,

19:34.170 --> 19:38.470
this guy's the type of monster 
you'd better steer clear of.

19:38.990 --> 19:41.150
<i>You may be right.</i>

19:41.400 --> 19:45.450
But I think Misaki-chan is about to wake up.

19:45.450 --> 19:48.200
Would you hurry back to 
this abandoned building?

19:48.200 --> 19:51.550
For real? She's seriously gonna wake up?

19:56.980 --> 19:59.380
<b>Present Time</b>

19:58.450 --> 19:59.610
Wait, what?

19:59.610 --> 20:00.920
What's going on?

20:00.920 --> 20:04.290
Hey, what do you mean I'm dead?

20:04.290 --> 20:06.890
I don't get it. Fill me in.

20:06.890 --> 20:10.630
So, even in such an advanced nation,

20:10.630 --> 20:13.930
children still suffer from 
disasters and circumstance.

20:14.850 --> 20:18.320
What would it take to find peace here?

20:19.200 --> 20:23.150
What exactly does "peace" mean to you?

20:23.150 --> 20:24.110
What?

20:24.110 --> 20:25.450
Let me see...

20:25.780 --> 20:30.590
For the "peace" I recommend, 
you would need...

20:31.210 --> 20:32.690
money.

20:32.690 --> 20:34.420
Too raw.

20:35.060 --> 20:38.820
Money? I suppose that's true in any land.

20:39.420 --> 20:43.880
Who are you? Or perhaps I should ask...

20:44.420 --> 20:48.610
What do you <i>want</i>? 
What's your goal in this city?

20:50.260 --> 20:53.460
I don't know the first 
thing about this place.

20:54.130 --> 20:58.800
But if I'm really the only necromancer here,

20:58.800 --> 21:01.280
I'd like to use my magic to earn money.

21:01.910 --> 21:04.240
I want power and a place to belong

21:04.240 --> 21:08.880
so I can live in more perfectly 
undisturbed peace than anyone else.

21:09.970 --> 21:13.410
In that case, why don't I lend you a hand?

21:14.500 --> 21:19.540
I'm Lisa Kuraki, 
an intermediary here in Shinjuku.

21:20.260 --> 21:24.650
It seems you're not Polka Shinoyama
 on the inside.

21:25.050 --> 21:30.760
As you've come from very far away, 
I'll be your bridge to this city.

21:31.240 --> 21:34.730
I'll assign people to help 
you adjust to life here.

21:35.230 --> 21:38.770
Misaki-chan and Takumi-kun.

21:38.770 --> 21:40.020
Huh?

23:14.730 --> 23:19.410
<i>As you've come from very far away, 
I'll be your bridge to this city.</i>

23:20.160 --> 23:23.550
<i>I'll assign people to help 
you adjust to life here.</i>

23:24.090 --> 23:27.230
<i>Misaki-chan and Takumi-kun.</i>

23:27.230 --> 23:28.010
Huh?

23:30.890 --> 23:34.050
Seriously, how'd I end up in this mess?
